":"numbered by first appearance in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the first vertex has colour 0, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour first appears after the one below it). It is the colouring "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"search finds, so it costs the same: a bipartite graph gets its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0), and each other component the colouring that DSatur branch and bound found for it, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greedy DSatur’s when that already uses no more colours than another component needs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sage "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex_coloring()"},{"type":"text","text":" and JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BrownBacktrackColoring.getColoring"},{"type":"text","text":", which also return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the optimal colouring their search finds; Mathematica "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindVertexColoring"},{"type":"text","text":". Deterministic, but which optimal colouring it is depends on the search; for one fixed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by a rule, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":". Exponential in the worst case, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":" is; the search does not check for task cancellation."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumColoring()":{"title":"minimumColoring()","url